# Dev Notes 23 — Worker Layout Option C Disposal Primitives v1

## Date

2026-06-07

## Branch

```text
worker-layout-option-c-disposal-primitives-v1
```

## Purpose

This branch resumes the paused Worker Layout Option C disposal-primitives slice after the inherited real-runtime context-cancel shutdown timeout fix landed on `modularization`.

It keeps `llama_worker/llama.mjs` as the stable worker entrypoint and composition root while extracting only small worker leaf helpers for:

- session/context disposal primitives;
- context option projection and terminal context-creation error construction;
- prompt token chunk factory creation.

## Source base

Implementation was staged from the updated formatted mirror:

```text
/mnt/data/runtime-dev-repo-modularization.zip
/mnt/data/resume_disposal_work/base/runtime-dev-repo-modularization
```

The mirror includes the completed real-runtime shutdown bugfix baseline:

```text
llama_worker/lifecycle/modelDisposalPolicy.mjs
tests/smokeTestWorkerModelDisposalPolicy.mjs
tests/smokeTestRealRuntimeContextCancelShutdownDiagnostics.mjs
```

This branch was manually reapplied onto that updated base. The old paused disposal-primitives patch was not applied wholesale because `llama_worker/llama.mjs` changed in the shared disposal area.

## Important bugfix interaction preserved

The inherited real-runtime shutdown bugfix made model disposal policy operation-aware:

```text
resetModel -> disposeModelStack({ operation: "reset_model" })
shutdownWorker -> disposeModelStack({ operation: "shutdown" })
```

This branch preserves that distinction. The new session-disposal helper is only passed `workerState.sessions`; it does not own model disposal policy, reset/shutdown operation selection, or terminal model-dispose abandonment behavior.

## Explicit non-goals preserved

This branch does not include:

- cancellation-core extraction;
- active-request registry extraction;
- request-boundary extraction;
- context retry service extraction;
- session service extraction;
- model/reset/shutdown lifecycle extraction;
- prompt runner extraction;
- worker protocol router extraction;
- parent runtime changes;
- worker protocol redesign;
- model path/model identity behavior changes;
- configOverride surface changes;
- prompt/output semantic changes;
- cleanup or optimization outside the narrow extraction.

