## Implementation summary

### Session disposal primitives

`llama_worker/session/sessionDisposal.mjs` exports:

```text
disposeSessionEntry(entry)
disposeSessionById(sessions, sessionId)
disposeAllSessions(sessions)
disposePartialSessionArtifacts({ session, context })
```

The extracted helpers preserve the existing disposal behavior:

- session disposal is attempted before context disposal;
- session disposal keeps `{ disposeSequence: true }`;
- context disposal remains awaited;
- cleanup errors are collected and the first error is thrown;
- all-session cleanup clears the sessions map after iterating;
- partial context/session cleanup uses the same session-first/context-second ordering.

The helpers accept the `sessions` map as an injected argument and do not import worker state, `llama.mjs`, or lifecycle services.

### Context options

`llama_worker/context/contextOptions.mjs` exports:

```text
toContextCreateOptions(contextConfig)
buildContextCreationError({ sessionId, attemptedProfiles, lastError })
```

The context creation option projection preserves the same keys:

```text
contextSize
batchSize
threads
flashAttention
performanceTracking
sequences
failedCreationRemedy
ignoreMemorySafetyChecks
```

The terminal context-creation error preserves:

```text
err.sessionId
err.attemptedContextProfiles
err.lastError
```

`buildContextCreationObsoleteError()` remains inline in `llama_worker/llama.mjs` because it depends on request-obsolete state and worker reset/shutdown readiness.

### Chunk factory

`llama_worker/prompt/chunkFactory.mjs` exports:

```text
createChunkFactory(model)
```

The extracted helper preserves:

- per-prompt `lastTokens` closure;
- array-token detokenization path;
- numeric-token detokenization path;
- `slice(-8)` token-history behavior;
- fallback `String(t)` behavior.

